Node.js LTS and pnpm

Install:
  Install missing pnpm and Node.js LTS; configure PATH and create missing npm/npx links.

Upgrade:
  Update pnpm and Node.js LTS installed under PNPM_HOME.

Status:
  Report command locations and local Node.js/pnpm versions.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.

Configuration:
  PNPM_HOME: ~/.local/share/pnpm by default; a custom absolute path is persisted.
  Shell configuration adds PNPM_HOME/bin, PNPM_HOME, and ~/.local/bin to PATH.
  Open a new terminal after installation to load the environment.
